###############################################################################
### substs #######################################################(changed!!!)#
###############################################################################
# substs in format: subst <addr> <phone|host> [<wtime> [<flag>]]
# each field can be replaced with '-' for keep unchanged.
# supported flags:  (may be only one flag for each subst!)
#	binkp - can Binkp calls to node,
#	ifc - can ifcico calls to node.
# on ip calls field <phone> must contain ip-addr, or host of node, or
# '-' to resolve the host in this order (FTS-5001, same as binkd):
#   1. hostname or IP written on this subst line
#   2. nodelist IBN:host when the flag is binkp, or IFC:host when it is ifc
#   3. nodelist INA:host
#   4. phone 000-A-B-C-D, read as IPv4 A.B.C.D
#   5. DNS f910.n203.z2.<suffix> for node 2:203/910
#      suffix is the nodelist IRD: flag, otherwise `rootdomain'
#      (qico.conf; default binkp.net)
# A non-default port on IBN:, IFC: or INA: is kept
# (BinkP default 24554, ifcico 60179).
#
# ex:
# Each block is a separate illustration. A repeated address here is not
# a hidden dialine; see the last pair for that.
#
# address: 1:2345/666, host: fido.foobar.com, prot: binkp; main line.
# subst	1:2345/666	fido.foobar.com		CM 		binkp
#
# address: 1:2345/666, nodelist IBN:binkp.example.com, flag binkp → host binkp.example.com
# subst	1:2345/666	-			CM		binkp
#
# address: 1:2345/123, nodelist IFC:ifc.example.com, flag ifc, wtime 23:30-8:00 → host ifc.example.com
# subst	1:2345/123	-			23:30-8:00	ifc
#
# address: 1:2345/666, nodelist INA:ina.example.com and no IBN:host, flag binkp → host ina.example.com
# subst	1:2345/666	-			CM		binkp
#
# address: 1:2345/666, nodelist phone 000-192-0-2-10, no IBN:host and no INA, flag binkp → host 192.0.2.10
# subst	1:2345/666	-			CM		binkp
#
# address: 2:203/910, no IBN:host, INA or 000-phone, flag binkp → host f910.n203.z2.binkp.net (`rootdomain')
# subst	2:203/910	-			CM		binkp
#
# address: 2:203/910, nodelist IRD:example.org and no host above, flag binkp → host f910.n203.z2.example.org
# subst	2:203/910	-			CM		binkp
#
# address: 1:2345/666, nodelist INA:fido.example.com,IBN:24555, flag binkp → host fido.example.com:24555
# subst	1:2345/666	-			CM		binkp
#
# address: 1:2345/546, phone: 123-4567, prot: emsi via modem.
# subst	1:2345/546	123-4567		-		-
#
# address: 1:2345/666, phone: from nodelist, prot: emsi via modem; hidden line.
# subst	1:2345/666	-			-
#
# Subst override nodelist, so for second (hidden) line you must specify
# two (or more) `subst':
# One for nodelist line
# subst 111:222/33		-			-
# One (ore more) for hidden line(s)
# subst 111:222/33		987-6543	18:00-9:00

# WARNING!
# translatesubst is off by default.
# In this case subst phones are used _WITHOUT_ translation!
# if translatesubst = yes, Subst phones are used _WITH_ translation!!!
;translatesubst	yes
